author: codex-sol
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Record the exact failed command and verify the current fix or upstream blocker without weakening tracker governance.
actual_result: "Merged in #208 as 38f8f1e; checks successful at head e4a8429: CodeQL, codeql, test (22), test (26), windows-acceptance-launcher (22), windows-acceptance-launcher (26). Review round AC acceptance dry-run (the item's registered command, run on the closeout worktree at current main) failed with exit code 1: the import gate reports the plan is not idempotent - 1 duplicate provenance tag in the existing corpus, 0 new entries without a provenance tag, 1 conflicting target; no item was written. An ungated dry run of the same import plans 6 imports, 5 updates and 0 skips."
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T10:46:53.041Z",codex-sol,"Run 43827565812 failed the pm-github 2026.11.4 idempotency gate: one shared provenance tag and one conflicting target. The shared #150 reference belongs to distinct pack-storage and crash-matrix tasks, so neither is a duplicate. pm-github 2026.11.15 separates references from explicit import ownership. Reuse open PR #208 and its caller pin; retain current main and verify the pinned dry-run. No item is closed."
  "2026-11-16T11:02:01.561Z",codex-sol,"Initial review receipt: the failed workflow log and current pin are documented in docs/issue-sync-2026-11-16.md. Seeded tracker validation passes through pm test --run --progress. Typecheck and lint pass. The quick package suite remains running under shared-host load; no complete passing suite is claimed.   Publish review evidence with pending gates explicit; no scheduled success is claimed."
  "2026-11-17T02:02:22.939Z",pi-glm,"Reopened in review round AC: the acceptance dry-run command registered on this item still fails on current main (exit code 1). The gate refuses the import plan as not idempotent - one duplicate provenance tag in the existing corpus and one conflicting target - so the duplicate-provenance repair delivered by PR 208 does not fully clear the scheduled sync's gate. No item was written by the dry run. The follow-up should identify the conflicting target and either repair its provenance tag or deduplicate the corpus entry before the next scheduled sync."
